From ae6679881ed3a6010d0361baa5d70724bec182ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: barracuda156 <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:18:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 68/70] maglev: ppc32 bodies for the 64-bit-only nodes of the
 ppc Maglev backend

maglev-ir-ppc.cc, the node half of the ppc backend, uses XER-based
overflow detection through mcrxrx (ISA 3.0, POWER9), 64-bit register
canonicalization (extsw), 64-bit FPU and POWER5+ instructions, none
of which a G3/G4/G5 has in 32-bit mode.  Give the affected nodes ppc32
bodies under #if V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC64 / #else; the ppc64 text is
unchanged.

- The 17 `extsw(out, out)` re-canonicalizations become
  SignExtend32To64Bits(out, out): extsw on ppc64 (same code), empty on
  ppc32, as on arm.

- Int32AddWithOverflow / Int32SubtractWithOverflow: upstream does
  `add/sub SetOE; mcrxrx; deopt overflow32`.  Use the macro
  assembler's xor-sign AddAndCheckForOverflow / SubAndCheckForOverflow
  (TurboFan's kPPC_AddWithOverflow32/SubWithOverflow32 helpers) with a
  masm scratch for the overflow word and r0 as their scratch; overflow
  is cr0 lt.  Both handle dst aliasing either input; Sub needs the
  dst == left == right fix from the macro-assembler commit for `a - a`.

- Int32Increment/Decrement/Negate/AbsWithOverflow: compare against
  kMaxInt/kMinInt and deopt before computing (x + 1 overflows only for
  kMaxInt, x - 1, -x and |x| only for kMinInt), then addi/neg.  The
  deopt happens before `out` is written.

- Int32MultiplyWithOverflow: upstream uses `mullw SetOE SetRC` and
  deopts on `overflow`, which on PowerPC is CR0[SO], a copy of the
  sticky XER[SO]: once any OE instruction overflowed on the thread it
  deopts forever (see below).  Its -0 test also reads left and right
  after mullw wrote `out`, which may alias one of them, so (-5) * 0
  with out == left produced +0.  ppc32 takes arm's shape: mulhw/mullw
  into scratch high/low words (low word in `out` unless it aliases an
  input), overflow iff high != low >> 31 (as TurboFan's
  kPPC_Mul32WithHigh32), then the -0 test on the intact inputs
  (or. of left and right, negative means -0), then move to `out`.

- Int32DivideWithOverflow: upstream's `divw LeaveOE SetRC` followed by
  `deopt overflow` tests only the stale sticky SO bit (OE is off); the
  deferred pre-checks already exclude x / 0, 0 / negative and
  kMinInt / -1.  The remainder check reads left and right after divw
  wrote `out`; with out aliasing an input (x / y where x dies) it
  computes q - q * y and deopts on exact divisions.  ppc32 divides
  into a scratch when `out` aliases an input, as arm does, and has no
  overflow deopt.

- Float64Round: frin/frip/frim/fcpsgn are ISA 2.02+/2.05.  The graph
  builder asks IsSupported(CpuOperation::kFloat64Round), which is
  false for ppc32, before creating the node (Math.round/floor/ceil/
  trunc, the Float64 Math.clz32 path, Uint8Clamped stores); the ppc32
  body is UNREACHABLE so a future change fails loudly instead of
  raising SIGILL.

- Float64Sqrt: fsqrt is optional and absent on G3/G4.  The generic
  commit made the node a call node on ppc32; the body calls
  ExternalReference::ieee754_sqrt_function() (the reference the series
  uses for TurboFan's Float64Sqrt) with the input fixed in d1, the
  Darwin FP argument and return register, the way
  Float64Ieee754Unary does.

- Float64Modulus: now a call node on ppc (generic commit); define its
  MaxCallStackArgs (0, as Float64Exponentiate).

- CheckedIntPtrToInt32: an IntPtr is an Int32 on 32-bit targets; empty
  body, as on arm (the lowered 32-bit compares would be dead).

- CheckFloat64SameValue against +-0: upstream compares all 64 bits.
  Once the value compared equal to zero, its low word is zero and the
  high word carries the sign, so compare the high word
  (MovDoubleHighToInt), as arm does.

Latent ppc64 defects seen while deriving the bodies, not changed here
(the ppc64 text is left as upstream has it): sticky XER[SO] in the
Multiply and Divide overflow deopts, the aliasing in the Multiply -0
test and in the Divide remainder check; details in the port's Maglev
design document.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 v8/src/maglev/ppc/maglev-ir-ppc.cc | 157 +++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 140 insertions(+), 17 deletions(-)

diff --git a/v8/src/maglev/ppc/maglev-ir-ppc.cc b/v8/src/maglev/ppc/maglev-ir-ppc.cc
index 813acc7..3f08350 100644
--- a/v8/src/maglev/ppc/maglev-ir-ppc.cc
+++ b/v8/src/maglev/ppc/maglev-ir-ppc.cc
@@ -32,14 +32,21 @@ void Int32NegateWithOverflow::GenerateCode(MaglevAssembler* masm,
   __ CmpS32(value, Operand::Zero(), r0);
   __ EmitEagerDeoptIf(eq, DeoptimizeReason::kOverflow, this);
 
+#if V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC64
     __ neg(out, value, SetOE);
     __ MoveToCrFromXer(cr0);
     // Output register must not be a register input into the eager deopt info.
     DCHECK_REGLIST_EMPTY(RegList{out} &
                          GetGeneralRegistersUsedAsInputs(eager_deopt_info()));
     __ EmitEagerDeoptIf(overflow32, DeoptimizeReason::kOverflow, this);
+#else
+  // No mcrxrx (ISA 3.0): -x overflows only for kMinInt.
+  __ CmpS32(value, Operand(kMinInt), r0);
+  __ EmitEagerDeoptIf(eq, DeoptimizeReason::kOverflow, this);
+  __ neg(out, value);
+#endif
 
-  __ extsw(out, out);
+  __ SignExtend32To64Bits(out, out);
 }
 
